## S3 Storage Lens — Zero to Hero

**S3 Storage Lens** is an **S3 storage analytics and visibility service** that helps you understand **how your S3 storage is being used**, including storage size, object counts, activity, and cost-related trends.

Think of it as:

> **"A dashboard for understanding my S3 estate."**

---

## 1. Why do we need S3 Storage Lens?

Imagine your company has:

```text
AWS Account
│
├── 100 S3 Buckets
│   ├── application-data
│   ├── backups
│   ├── logs
│   ├── images
│   └── archives
│
├── Multiple Regions
│
└── Millions of objects
```

Now management asks:

> "Why is our S3 storage growing so quickly?"

or:

> "Which buckets have the most data?"

or:

> "How much data is in Standard vs Glacier?"

or:

> "Are we using S3 versioning and lifecycle features effectively?"

Checking every bucket manually would be painful.

### Storage Lens gives you centralized visibility.

```text
              S3 Storage Lens
                    │
       ┌────────────┼────────────┐
       ▼            ▼            ▼
    Buckets       Objects      Storage
       │            │            │
       └────────────┼────────────┘
                    ▼
               Dashboard
```

---

# 2. What can Storage Lens show?

It provides metrics around things such as:

### Storage

```text
Total storage
Object count
Average object size
```

### Storage classes

For example:

```text
S3 Standard        → 5 TB
Standard-IA        → 2 TB
Glacier             → 10 TB
Deep Archive        → 50 TB
```

This helps you understand your storage distribution.

### Activity

Depending on the metrics/configuration, you can analyze S3 usage such as:

```text
Requests
Data retrieval
Data transfer
```

### Data management

You can also get visibility into things such as:

```text
Versioning
Lifecycle
Incomplete multipart uploads
Delete markers
Replication
Encryption
```

The exact metrics available depend on the Storage Lens configuration and metric type.

