# 3. Real-time DevOps example ⭐

Suppose you work for an organization with:

```text
20 AWS accounts
200 S3 buckets
50 TB of data
```

After a few years:

```text
150 TB
```

The DevOps team wants to investigate.

You open:

```text
S3
 ↓
Storage Lens
 ↓
Dashboard
```

You discover:

```text
Bucket                  Storage
--------------------------------
prod-logs               70 TB
application-data        30 TB
backups                 40 TB
images                  10 TB
other                    0 TB
```

Now you investigate `prod-logs`.

You discover:

```text
70 TB
│
├── 10 TB → Standard
├── 20 TB → Standard-IA
└── 40 TB → Glacier
```

This gives you **visibility into your S3 environment**.

