# 🎯 Interview questions

### Q1. What is S3 Storage Lens?

> S3 Storage Lens is an S3 analytics capability that provides centralized visibility into S3 storage usage, activity, and trends across buckets, accounts, and Regions.

### Q2. Does Storage Lens move objects?

> No. Storage Lens provides analytics and visibility. Lifecycle rules are used to automatically transition or expire objects.

### Q3. Storage Lens vs Inventory?

> Storage Lens provides aggregated analytics and trends about S3 usage, whereas S3 Inventory provides scheduled object-level inventory information.

### Q4. Storage Lens vs CloudWatch?

> CloudWatch is a general AWS monitoring service, whereas S3 Storage Lens is specifically focused on analyzing S3 storage usage and activity.

### 🧠 One-line memory trick

```text
S3 Storage Lens = "LOOK at my S3 environment"
S3 Inventory    = "LIST my S3 objects"
Lifecycle       = "MOVE/DELETE my S3 objects automatically"
CloudWatch      = "MONITOR AWS resources and applications"
```

For an **AWS DevOps interview**, this distinction is much more important than memorizing every individual Storage Lens metric.
